WEBVTT

00:00:00.256 --> 00:00:04.856
Open Advanced Automation, Scripts, Change Virtual Switch MTU

00:00:04.864 --> 00:00:09.336
as an administrator. This standalone action targets the default V S

00:00:09.344 --> 00:00:13.128
zero, or B R zero, on the supported healthy cluster.

00:00:13.258 --> 00:00:17.815
Unlike the PE-direct uplink wizard, this workflow uses trusted PE

00:00:17.866 --> 00:00:21.990
and Prism Central connections and the supported PC networking API.

00:00:22.284 --> 00:00:26.265
Review the intended cluster UUID, saved credentials,

00:00:26.337 --> 00:00:30.084
active-backup bond and physical network support for jumbo frames.

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:33.336
Confirm maintenance capacity and out-of-band access.

00:00:33.609 --> 00:00:37.697
The reviewed change raises the physical uplink MTU from fifteen hundred

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:41.523
to nine thousand while preserving the existing bond and uplinks.

00:00:41.886 --> 00:00:46.069
Run read-only preflight and inspect every host and physical uplink.

00:00:46.257 --> 00:00:49.364
Missing or inconsistent readback blocks application.

00:00:49.713 --> 00:00:54.100
Have another administrator approve the exact plan, then use the cluster-bound

00:00:54.108 --> 00:00:57.629
confirmation only in a separately validated environment.

00:00:57.752 --> 00:00:59.664
Live writes default to off;

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:02.537
this demonstration performs no MTU changes.

00:01:02.957 --> 00:01:06.640
Follow the Prism task and per-host readback in Jobs and Queue.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:10.808
Keep controller virtual machine interface MTU at fifteen hundred as

00:01:10.808 --> 00:01:14.908
documented. Verify end-to-end traffic on the intended VLANs

00:01:14.916 --> 00:01:19.516
separately. A successful task alone does not prove that the physical switching path

00:01:19.524 --> 00:01:21.393
carries jumbo frames correctly.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:24.428
Reconcile the original Prism task first.

00:01:24.655 --> 00:01:28.615
Enter the settled change job identifier and review the recorded original

00:01:28.751 --> 00:01:31.602
MTU against current identity and settings.

00:01:31.695 --> 00:01:34.748
Request fresh rollback approval and confirmation.

00:01:34.958 --> 00:01:39.046
If telemetry is unavailable, use the site console recovery procedure;

00:01:39.097 --> 00:01:42.578
the workflow does not automatically reverse an uncertain write.
